<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Władysław II the Exile</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1105–1159</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Władysław II the Exile was the eldest son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boleslaw-iii-wrymouth">Bolesław III Wrymouth</a> and, under his father's testament of 1138, High Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> and Duke of Silesia. His attempt to dispossess his younger half-brothers failed, and in 1146 they drove him into exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, where he died in 1159. With imperial backing his sons recovered Silesia in 1163, founding the Silesian line of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piast-dynasty">Piasts</a>.</p></div>
